---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# Full-text search where the web UI offers it outside ⌘K's own list: the
# sidebar filter (which reads transcripts as well as titles) and the
# palette's Wiki group, and where a hit takes you. Recipe:
# go/tests/model/README.md. ui_sidebar.fizz models the filter as
# title-only and ui_palette.fizz has no wiki and no failing wiki; this
# flow is the part between them.
#
# Code this is checked against (go/internal/serve):
#   web/src/app.tsx      getSearchMatch (the local hit: title, branch,
#                        repo, path, id); App's useFullText(query, true),
#                        `said` and `visible` (a row is listed for a local
#                        hit or a transcript hit); Sidebar's row reasons
#                        ("said: …"), "No sessions match", the "N more
#                        found in the conversation · ⌘K" link
#                        (saidElsewhere), the empty-row rule (an empty,
#                        dead session lists only for a query), Archived's
#                        "Include" (archFromFilter), onSelect's jump to
#                        the line that said it; closePalette, goWiki.
#   web/src/palette.tsx  useFullText (180 ms debounce, abort, the forQ
#                        guard), useWikiHits (180 ms debounce, no guard),
#                        the Mentioned in and Wiki groups, "Text search
#                        failed · Retry", pick/afterClose.
#   serve/search.go      GET /api/search (searchLimit 25)
#   serve/wiki.go        GET /api/wiki/search (limit 8)
#
# The fixture behind the abstract values: sessions
#   A  a title (set by rename) holding "title"; its transcript does not.
#   B  a transcript line (seq n) holding "said"; no title, branch, repo,
#      path or id holds it.
#   E  empty and dead (never prompted, not open), in a folder whose path
#      holds "title": a path hit, listed only while a query asks for it.
#   Z  archived; a transcript line holding "arch".
# and one wiki page W, one of whose claims mentions "said" and nothing
# else typed here. Queries: "short" is one character nothing holds (the
# transcripts are not read under two), "none" is a phrase nothing holds.
#
# The mapped states are field values:
#   off                          field False
#   typed_short                  query "short"
#   debouncing, searching        search "loading" (one state: see below)
#   done_title_hit               query "title", search "done"
#   done_said_hit                "B" (or "Z") in said and in rows
#   done_elsewhere               elsewhere 1
#   done_nomatch                 note "nomatch"
#   search_failed_shown_as_nomatch   what the product does today (below);
#                                owed: note "failed"
#   stale_answer                 said/found/wikiRows for another query
#                                (owed never; see Hits*Current)
#   opened_at_line               open B or Z, at "line"
#   palette_wiki_hits_previous_query  wikiRows ["W"] with pq != "said"
#   palette_wiki_failed_empty    wiki "error" with wikiSays ""
#   palette_hit_picked           page "W", or open from the palette
#
# Corrections to the mapped model, from the code:
# - Debouncing and searching are one state. useFullText sets "loading" as
#   the key lands, before the 180 ms timer, and nothing on the page tells
#   the timer from the request; DebounceFires is not an action.
# - A stale answer never lands in the session search: a newer query
#   aborts the older read and the forQ guard drops an answer for another
#   query, so typing clears `said`/`found` at once. The stale case is the
#   Wiki group's alone (useWikiHits keeps its hits until the new answer).
# - Poll is not an action: the list poll re-renders the rows but neither
#   search re-runs on it (their deps are the query and Retry), so nothing
#   here changes.
# - The palette's wiki hit carries no cite: WikiHit is {path, title,
#   topic, excerpt, counts} and the pick calls goWiki({at: "page", path}).
#   "Opens its page and cite" is not what the server can answer; the
#   model asserts the page (gap below).
#
# WHAT THIS SPEC OWES THAT THE PRODUCT DOES NOT DO TODAY. Each line is a
# mutation that turns the spec into today's product and makes fizz fail
# on the named assertion (see the report); stage 2/3 walks will be red
# here until the product is fixed:
# 1. Sidebar, failed search: App discards useFullText's state, so a
#    failure reads "No sessions match" with no Retry. Owed: "Text search
#    failed · Retry" (note "failed"). -> FailureIsSaid
# 2. Sidebar, in flight: with nothing matched locally the list says "No
#    sessions match" while the transcripts are still being read. Owed:
#    "Searching…" (note "searching"). -> NoMatchOnlySettled
# 3. Palette, Wiki group: useWikiHits keeps the previous query's pages
#    for 180 ms plus the round trip after every keystroke, and Enter or a
#    click then opens a page that does not match. Owed: hits belong to the
#    query on screen (the useDirs/forQ guard). -> WikiHitsCurrent
# 4. Palette, failed wiki search: the group silently empties while the
#    session search says "Text search failed". Owed: the failure said
#    (wikiSays "failed"). -> FailureIsSaid
# 5. Palette, a Mentioned in row for a session the list holds (B): its
#    run is onOpenSession(r.id) with no seq, so it opens at the end, not
#    at the line; only a hit the list does not hold (Z) jumps. Owed: the
#    line. -> SaidOpensAtLine
#
# Product gaps not modelled (notes, not claims):
# - searchLimit 25: the sidebar asks with no limit, so a phrase said in
#   more than 25 sessions silently lists 25 and says nothing of the rest.
# - A said-only hit on a session the palette's `listable` drops (a
#   background agent whose parent is listed) is filtered out of `texts`
#   in the palette but counted in the sidebar.
# - Wiki pick has no cite (above).
#
# Pruned, because every generated path is one browser test:
# - A session is opened only from a filtered list (the flow is about
#   search), and while one is open, or the wiki page is, only Back is
#   walked: the sidebar under it behaves as from the list.
# - The palette opens from a quiet sidebar only: ⌘K with the filter
#   empty, or the "more found" link (query "arch", answered). While it is
#   up the sidebar's own search is settled and nothing else moves.
# - In the palette only "said", "none" and Clear are typed ("arch" comes
#   from the link): together they are every wiki answer (a page, none,
#   stale, failed) and both Mentioned in kinds (listed B, unlisted Z).
# - The palette's Start, commands and arrows are ui_palette's.
# - Archived's own load (loading/failed) is ui_sidebar's: Include lists
#   Z at once. Include is offered only under a query, so it always ends
#   with the query (archFromFilter).
#
# Fairness: the server answering (SearchOk, PSearchOk, WikiAnswer) is
# weakly fair; failures and the person are not. Weak suffices: typing
# again keeps the answer enabled (loading stays loading), and a failure
# leaves "loading" behind, which is all the liveness claims ask for, so
# failing forever is no violation. The claims are one per read (below):
# a single "all three settled" claim is false, since a person typing
# between the palette's two answers forever never has both at once.

# What each query's transcript search answers (ids, in list order).
def transcriptHits(q):
    if q == "said":
        return ["B"]
    if q == "arch":
        return ["Z"]
    return []

# The local hit (getSearchMatch): A's title and E's path hold "title".
def localHits(q):
    if q == "title":
        return ["A", "E"]
    return []

# The sessions the page's `rows` holds: Z only once Archived is shown.
def listedIds(s):
    if s.archived:
        return ["A", "B", "E", "Z"]
    return ["A", "B", "E"]

# Nothing in front of the sidebar: no session, wiki page or palette.
def quiet(s):
    return s.open == "" and s.page == "" and not s.palette

role Search:
    action Init:
        # --- the sidebar filter ---
        # The filter field is shown (Filter button or "/").
        self.field = False
        # "empty" | "short" | "title" | "said" | "arch" | "none"
        self.query = "empty"
        # useFullText as the sidebar gets it: idle (no query, or under two
        # characters) | loading | done | error.
        self.search = "idle"
        # The sessions whose transcript answered the query on screen.
        self.said = []
        # Archived shown (from the filter's Include).
        self.archived = False
        # --- the thread / wiki page ---
        # The open session ("" none) and where it opened: "top" (as any
        # open does) or "line" (scrolled to the line that said it, marked).
        self.open = ""
        self.at = ""
        # The wiki page open from the palette ("" none).
        self.page = ""
        # --- the palette ---
        self.palette = False
        # "empty" | "said" | "none" | "arch"
        self.pq = "empty"
        # The palette's session search and the rows it answered.
        self.psearch = "idle"
        self.found = []
        # The palette's wiki search and the pages its Wiki group lists.
        self.wiki = "idle"
        self.wikiRows = []
        # --- derived (recompute) ---
        # The sidebar's rows: listed sessions, the Archived section's too.
        self.rows = []
        # What the list says besides rows: "" | "searching" | "failed" |
        # "nomatch".
        self.note = ""
        # The "N more found in the conversation" link's N.
        self.elsewhere = 0
        # What the Wiki group says when it lists nothing: "" | "failed".
        self.wikiSays = ""
        self.recompute()

    atomic func recompute():
        listed = listedIds(self)
        rows = []
        if self.query == "empty":
            # E is empty and dead: hidden with no query.
            rows = [i for i in listed if i != "E"]
        else:
            rows = [i for i in listed if i in localHits(self.query) or i in self.said]
        self.rows = rows
        self.elsewhere = len([i for i in self.said if i not in listed])
        note = ""
        if self.query != "empty":
            if self.search == "error":
                note = "failed"
            elif len(rows) == 0 and self.search == "loading":
                note = "searching"
            elif len(rows) == 0:
                note = "nomatch"
        self.note = note
        self.wikiSays = "failed" if self.palette and self.wiki == "error" else ""

    # A new query: a transcript read for two characters or more, and the
    # previous answer gone at once (the forQ guard).
    atomic func setQuery(q):
        self.query = q
        self.said = []
        self.search = "idle" if q in ["empty", "short"] else "loading"
        if q == "empty":
            # Include lasts as long as the filter.
            self.archived = False

    # --- the sidebar filter ---------------------------------------------

    # The toolbar's Filter button, or "/".
    atomic action OpenFilter:
        require quiet(self) and not self.field
        self.field = True
        self.recompute()

    atomic action TypeShort:
        require quiet(self) and self.field and self.query != "short"
        self.setQuery("short")
        self.recompute()

    atomic action TypeTitle:
        require quiet(self) and self.field and self.query != "title"
        self.setQuery("title")
        self.recompute()

    atomic action TypeSaid:
        require quiet(self) and self.field and self.query != "said"
        self.setQuery("said")
        self.recompute()

    atomic action TypeArch:
        require quiet(self) and self.field and self.query != "arch"
        self.setQuery("arch")
        self.recompute()

    atomic action TypeNone:
        require quiet(self) and self.field and self.query != "none"
        self.setQuery("none")
        self.recompute()

    # Select all, delete: the field stays.
    atomic action Clear:
        require quiet(self) and self.field and self.query != "empty"
        self.setQuery("empty")
        self.recompute()

    # Escape in the field: query cleared, field hidden.
    atomic action Escape:
        require quiet(self) and self.field
        self.setQuery("empty")
        self.field = False
        self.recompute()

    atomic fair action SearchOk:
        require self.search == "loading"
        self.search = "done"
        self.said = transcriptHits(self.query)
        self.recompute()

    atomic action SearchFails:
        require self.search == "loading"
        self.search = "error"
        self.said = []
        self.recompute()

    # The owed "Text search failed · Retry".
    atomic action Retry:
        require quiet(self) and self.note == "failed"
        self.search = "loading"
        self.recompute()

    # Archived's "Include" under a query, and its fold back.
    atomic action ToggleArchived:
        require quiet(self) and self.query != "empty"
        self.archived = not self.archived
        self.recompute()

    # A row listed for a local hit: opens as any open does.
    atomic action SelectTitleRow:
        require quiet(self) and self.query != "empty"
        require len([i for i in self.rows if i in localHits(self.query)]) > 0
        self.open = [i for i in self.rows if i in localHits(self.query)][0]
        self.at = "top"
        self.recompute()

    # A row listed only for what it said: opens at that line (setJump).
    atomic action SelectSaidRow:
        require quiet(self) and self.query != "empty"
        require len([i for i in self.rows if i not in localHits(self.query)]) > 0
        self.open = [i for i in self.rows if i not in localHits(self.query)][0]
        self.at = "line"
        self.recompute()

    # "1 more found in the conversation · ⌘K": the palette, seeded with
    # the query.
    atomic action OpenElsewhere:
        require quiet(self) and self.query != "empty" and self.elsewhere > 0
        self.palette = True
        self.pq = self.query
        self.psearch = "loading"
        self.found = []
        self.wiki = "loading"
        self.wikiRows = []
        self.recompute()

    # Browser Back from the session or the wiki page to the list; the
    # filter is as it was.
    atomic action Back:
        require self.open != "" or self.page != ""
        self.open = ""
        self.at = ""
        self.page = ""
        self.recompute()

    # --- the palette ------------------------------------------------------

    # ⌘K from a quiet sidebar with no filter.
    atomic action OpenPalette:
        require quiet(self) and self.query == "empty"
        self.palette = True
        self.pq = "empty"
        self.psearch = "idle"
        self.found = []
        self.wiki = "idle"
        self.wikiRows = []
        self.recompute()

    # A new palette query: both reads start, both answers for the old
    # query gone (owed for the wiki: gap 3).
    atomic func setPq(q):
        self.pq = q
        self.found = []
        self.wikiRows = []
        if q == "empty":
            self.psearch = "idle"
            self.wiki = "idle"
        else:
            self.psearch = "loading"
            self.wiki = "loading"

    atomic action PTypeSaid:
        require self.palette and self.pq != "said"
        self.setPq("said")
        self.recompute()

    atomic action PTypeNone:
        require self.palette and self.pq != "none"
        self.setPq("none")
        self.recompute()

    atomic action PClear:
        require self.palette and self.pq != "empty"
        self.setPq("empty")
        self.recompute()

    atomic fair action PSearchOk:
        require self.palette and self.psearch == "loading"
        self.psearch = "done"
        self.found = transcriptHits(self.pq)
        self.recompute()

    atomic action PSearchFails:
        require self.palette and self.psearch == "loading"
        self.psearch = "error"
        self.found = []
        self.recompute()

    # "Text search failed · Retry" in the palette.
    atomic action PRetry:
        require self.palette and self.psearch == "error"
        self.psearch = "loading"
        self.recompute()

    atomic fair action WikiAnswer:
        require self.palette and self.wiki == "loading"
        self.wiki = "done"
        self.wikiRows = ["W"] if self.pq == "said" else []
        self.recompute()

    atomic action WikiFail:
        require self.palette and self.wiki == "loading"
        self.wiki = "error"
        self.wikiRows = []
        self.recompute()

    atomic func closePalette():
        self.palette = False
        self.pq = "empty"
        self.psearch = "idle"
        self.found = []
        self.wiki = "idle"
        self.wikiRows = []

    # A Mentioned in row: the session, at the line that said it (owed for
    # a listed session: gap 5).
    atomic action PickSession:
        require self.palette and len(self.found) > 0
        self.open = self.found[0]
        self.at = "line"
        self.closePalette()
        self.recompute()

    # A Wiki row (Enter when it leads, or a click): its page.
    atomic action PickWikiHit:
        require self.palette and "W" in self.wikiRows
        self.page = self.wikiRows[0]
        self.closePalette()
        self.recompute()

    atomic action PEscape:
        require self.palette
        self.closePalette()
        self.recompute()

action Init:
    s = Search()

# A failed search is said, never shown as "No sessions match" or as an
# empty Wiki group.
always assertion FailureIsSaid:
    if s.search == "error" and s.note != "failed":
        return False
    return not (s.palette and s.wiki == "error" and s.wikiSays != "failed")

# "No sessions match" only once the transcripts have answered (or were
# never asked: under two characters).
always assertion NoMatchOnlySettled:
    return s.note != "nomatch" or s.search in ["idle", "done"]

# Transcript hits belong to the query on screen, in both lists.
always assertion HitsCurrent:
    if s.search != "done" and len(s.said) > 0:
        return False
    if len([i for i in s.said if i not in transcriptHits(s.query)]) > 0:
        return False
    if s.psearch != "done" and len(s.found) > 0:
        return False
    return len([i for i in s.found if i not in transcriptHits(s.pq)]) == 0

# The Wiki group lists only pages that answer the query on screen, so
# Enter never opens a page for a query no longer typed.
always assertion WikiHitsCurrent:
    return len(s.wikiRows) == 0 or (s.wiki == "done" and s.pq == "said")

# A session listed only for what it said opens at its line; a local hit
# opens as any open does. B and Z hold no query's local hit, A and E no
# transcript hit, so the session says which it was.
always assertion SaidOpensAtLine:
    if s.open in ["B", "Z"]:
        return s.at == "line"
    if s.open in ["A", "E"]:
        return s.at == "top"
    return s.open == "" and s.at == ""

# The "more found" link counts only the hits the list cannot show, and
# every hit the list can show is listed: Z once Archived is included.
always assertion ElsewhereCounts:
    listed = listedIds(s)
    shown = [i for i in s.said if i in s.rows]
    if s.elsewhere + len(shown) != len(s.said):
        return False
    return not (s.archived and "Z" in s.said and "Z" not in s.rows)

# With a filter, the empty dead session its query hits is listed.
always assertion FilterListsHidden:
    return s.query != "title" or "E" in s.rows

# Picking a wiki hit leaves the palette on its page.
always assertion WikiPickOpensPage:
    return s.page == "" or (s.page == "W" and not s.palette and s.open == "")

# Every query gets an answer or an error: each read settles. One claim
# per read, not one for all three at once: typing between the palette's
# session answer and its wiki answer, forever, never has both settled in
# the same state, and a person may do that; each read still answers.
always eventually assertion SidebarSettles:
    return s.search != "loading"

always eventually assertion PaletteSearchSettles:
    return s.psearch != "loading"

always eventually assertion WikiSettles:
    return s.wiki != "loading"
